<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

    <!-- False positive: CVE-2022-31691 is for Spring Tools 4 IDE (Eclipse/VSCode plugins),
         not spring-boot-devtools. The CPE matcher incorrectly matches on "spring_boot_tools". -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            CVE-2022-31691 affects Spring Tools 4 for Eclipse and VSCode extensions (Snakeyaml vulnerability),
            not spring-boot-devtools. spring-boot-devtools is also runtime+optional and excluded from production builds.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.springframework\.boot/spring\-boot\-devtools@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2022-31691</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--                                                                    
       CVE-2026-29062: Nesting Depth Constraint Bypass in UTF8DataInputJsonParser (CVSS 8.7)
       Fixed in Jackson 3.1.0, but Spring Boot 4.0.3 ships Jackson 3.0.4.
       Jackson 3.0.x is not LTS and will not receive a patch; Spring Boot will
       upgrade to Jackson 3.1 in a future release.                            
       Risk is mitigated: all JSON-accepting endpoints require authentication,   
       and @Valid DTOs are shallow structures that reject deeply-nested input.
       Tracking: https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/issues/36130
                 https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/issues/49365
       Suppress until: Spring Boot upgrades to Jackson 3.1+
   -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[                                                       
           Suppressed pending Spring Boot upgrade to Jackson 3.1+.
           All inbound JSON is behind authentication; flat DTOs limit nesting.
       ]]></notes>
        <cve>CVE-2026-29062</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        DOMPurify (bundled inside swagger-ui) XSS-bypass advisories. swagger-ui
        5.32.6 still ships a vulnerable DOMPurify (3.4.0) and there is no upstream
        fix yet. These CVE IDs rotate as new DOMPurify advisories are published;
        the older -15599/-0540 IDs no longer match the current jar, so the active
        set below is kept in sync with what dependency-check currently reports.
        All are Medium (CVSS ~4.0), and Swagger UI is disabled in production.
        Risk is mitigated: Swagger UI is restricted to non-production profiles only.
        Tracking: https://github.com/swagger-api/swagger-ui/issues/10478
        Suppress until: swagger-ui ships with a patched DOMPurify.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            Suppressed pending swagger-ui upgrade of bundled DOMPurify.
            Swagger UI is disabled in production profiles.
        ]]></notes>
        <filePath regex="true">.*swagger-ui.*\.jar.*</filePath>
        <cve>CVE-2025-15599</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-0540</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-49458</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-49459</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-49978</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        CVE-2026-0994: DoS via recursion depth bypass in protobuf ParseDict().
        This vulnerability is Python-only (google.protobuf.json_format.ParseDict).
        The Java protobuf library does not contain this code path.
        OWASP Dependency-Check matches the CVE to protobuf-java by artifact name.
        Suppress until: NVD corrects the CPE scope to exclude Java.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            Python-only vulnerability in protobuf json_format.ParseDict().
            Does not affect protobuf-java.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/com\.google\.protobuf/protobuf\-java.*@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-0994</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        CVE-2026-53914: Code execution via unsafe deserialization (CWE-502) in
        JetBrains Kotlin's BUILD CACHE metadata, fixed in Kotlin 2.4.20.
        The vulnerable code path is the Kotlin compiler / Gradle build cache,
        i.e. a build-time concern. broadcaster-service is a Java application;
        kotlin-stdlib is only a transitive RUNTIME dependency and never invokes
        the Kotlin build cache, so this is not reachable here.
        Dependency-Check stamps the jetbrains:kotlin CPE onto every
        org.jetbrains.kotlin jar by artifact name (kotlin-stdlib, kotlin-reflect,
        kotlin-stdlib-common, etc.), so this match is scoped to the whole
        org.jetbrains.kotlin group rather than a single artifact.
        Suppress until: the transitive Kotlin artifacts are at 2.4.20+.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            CVE-2026-53914 is Kotlin build-cache deserialization (build-time).
            This is a Java runtime service; the Kotlin artifacts are transitive
            and never invoke the build cache.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.jetbrains\.kotlin/.*@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-53914</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        CVE-2025-46392: Uncontrolled resource consumption (DoS) in Apache
        Commons Configuration 1.x when loading UNTRUSTED configuration. Apache
        will NOT fix 1.x; the only remediation is migrating to commons-configuration2
        (different groupId + Java package), which is not a drop-in.
        This is a load-bearing transitive: twitch4j-helix wraps its Feign HTTP
        clients with Netflix Hystrix, which uses Netflix Archaius, which is built
        directly on commons-configuration 1.x. It cannot be excluded or upgraded
        without breaking Twitch4J's HTTP layer.
        Not exploitable here: commons-configuration is used internally by Archaius
        with trusted config only; no attacker-controlled configuration is loaded.
        Matches Apache's guidance that 1.x is safe for trusted configs.
        Suppress until: Twitch4J drops Hystrix/Archaius or moves to commons-configuration2.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            CVE-2025-46392 only affects untrusted-config loading. Here
            commons-configuration is an internal, load-bearing transitive of
            Twitch4J's Hystrix/Archaius HTTP plumbing; only trusted config is
            loaded. Cannot be upgraded (1.x is won't-fix; 2.x is a different
            package Archaius can't use).
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/commons-configuration/commons-configuration@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2025-46392</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        CVE-2026-66299: Uncontrolled resource consumption (DoS) in Apache Tomcat
        (CVSS 7.5). Affects 11.0.0-M20 through 11.0.24, 10.1.24 through 10.1.57,
        and 9.0.89 through 9.0.120.

        Not applicable to embedded Tomcat. The vulnerability is in the WebSocket
        *chat example*, which ships in the `examples` web application of the
        standalone Tomcat distribution. The advisory states it directly:
        "Users who have followed the security guidance to remove the examples web
        application are not affected by this issue."

        Spring Boot embeds only the servlet container via the tomcat-embed-*
        artifacts, which contain no webapps at all — inspecting
        tomcat-embed-core-11.0.24.jar shows only jakarta/servlet, jakarta/security
        and org/apache packages, with zero entries for the examples application.
        There is therefore no code path to the vulnerable example.

        Cannot currently be fixed by upgrading: the advisory recommends 11.0.25 /
        10.1.58 / 9.0.121 "(when released)", and 11.0.25 is not yet published.
        Spring Boot 4.1.0 itself manages 11.0.24, so this is the newest available.

        Scoped to the tomcat-embed family because dependency-check's CPE matching
        attributes product-level Tomcat CVEs to any of core / el / websocket, and
        the reasoning above applies identically to all three.

        Suppress until: 11.0.25 is released and picked up (either via Spring Boot's
        managed version or an explicit tomcat.version property), then delete this
        entry — dependency-check will stop reporting it on its own once the version
        moves past 11.0.24, but leaving dead suppressions hides future findings.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            CVE-2026-66299 affects Tomcat's WebSocket chat example, which lives in the
            `examples` web application and is not present in the embedded distribution.
            Spring Boot ships only tomcat-embed-* (servlet container, no webapps), so the
            vulnerable code is absent — the advisory confirms installations without the
            examples webapp are unaffected. No fixed release exists yet (11.0.25 is
            "when released"); 11.0.24 is what Spring Boot 4.1.0 manages.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.tomcat\.embed/tomcat\-embed\-.*@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-66299</cve>
    </suppress>

</suppressions>